# What keeps this index the parent-workspace index.
#
# GitNexus decides what `analyze` sees from .gitignore, and .gitignore cannot
# hold this boundary: the fifteen sub-repos are submodules (ADR-031), and an
# ignored path is one `git submodule add` refuses. With those paths absent from
# .gitignore, an analyze here would pull all fifteen codebases into one index —
# thousands of files under the one registry name documented as holding none of
# them.
#
# This file holds the boundary instead. Each sub-repo has its OWN GitNexus
# index, registered under its own name — see docs/gitnexus.md for the
# registry-name table. Querying the platform's code through
# `fullstack-marketplace-blueprint` is always the wrong index, and this file is
# what stops it from being possible.
#
# ⚠️ Every new sub-repo needs a line here as well as a submodule entry. Verify
# after any analyze: `stats.files` in .gitnexus/meta.json must stay in the low
# hundreds. Thousands means a sub-repo got in.

BEs/
marketplace-admin/
marketplace-nginx/
marketplace-shopowner/
marketplace-user/
